Let \(f,g\in\Gamma_0(\mathcal H)\). Suppose at least one of the following holds:
(i) \((\forall y\in\operatorname{dom}\partial g)\;\partial g(y)\subset\partial g(\operatorname{Prox}_f y)\);
(ii) \((\forall(x,u)\in\operatorname{gra}\partial f)\;\partial g(x+u)\subset\partial g(x)\);
(iii) \(\operatorname{dom}g\) is open, \(g\) is Gâteaux differentiable on \(\operatorname{dom}g\), \(\operatorname{dom}\partial f\subset\operatorname{dom}g\), and \((\forall y\in\operatorname{dom}g)\;\nabla g(y)=\nabla g(\operatorname{Prox}_f y)\);
(iv) \(0\in\operatorname{sri}(\operatorname{dom}f-\operatorname{dom}g)\) and \((\forall(x,u)\in\operatorname{gra}\partial f)\;\partial g(x)\subset\partial g(x+u)\).
Then
\[
\operatorname{Prox}_{f+g}=\operatorname{Prox}_f\circ\operatorname{Prox}_g.
\]
